cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Teanga Bench"
message: "If you use Teanga Bench, its evaluation harness, or its published results, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Conway
    given-names: John
    affiliation: "Blas / Tonada"
version: "0.2.1"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24305705"
date-released: "2026-11-17"
license: Apache-2.0
comment: >-
  Apache-2.0 applies to the harness code, scripts, and documentation only.
  Public sample text in samples/ retains the per-item licence recorded on each
  row and in samples/LICENCE.md (including GPL-3.0 for Gaelg Manx sentences,
  CC BY 2.0 FR, CC BY 4.0, OGL-v3, CC BY-SA 4.0, and private app sample excerpts).
repository-code: "https://github.com/johnway114/teanga-bench"
repository-artifact: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/johnconway114/teanga-bench"
url: "https://research.blasapp.com"
abstract: >-
  Teanga Bench measures how well large language models perform the work of a
  language tutor across two suites: the Blas suite (Irish, Welsh, Scottish
  Gaelic, Manx, Breton, and Cornish) and the Tonada suite (English tutoring
  for Portuguese, Spanish, Vietnamese, and Japanese L1 learners).
keywords:
  - celtic-languages
  - irish
  - welsh
  - scottish-gaelic
  - manx
  - breton
  - cornish
  - english-tutoring
  - llm-evaluation
  - low-resource-languages
  - language-tutoring
  - benchmark
